Z||000000||V8Fiero||05-20-2001||08:23 PM||||While alot of people were enjoying the sunshine and nice weather in Carlise, I spent most of the weekend wrenching on the fiero.<P>Replaced the rear brake pads.<BR>Changed the oil pan gasket.<BR>Changed my radiator.<BR>Changed the water pump.<P>Id say that was a pretty full weekend.<BR>Imagine what the labor cost would have been if I couldnt do this stuff myself.....<P>Scott||||reg||6
Z||000001||Formula88||05-20-2001||09:46 PM||||WORD!  I spent a good bit of the weekend replacing my sail panel and pulling off a clogged catastrophic converter.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I like to never get that exhaust to seal since the old converter was welded in right at the curve of the pipe.  I didn't have any straight pipe to connect the new section to.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Oh, well, this is just a temp fix till I can get my new cat, SpinTech, and pipes from West Coast Fiero.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||thomas_l||05-21-2001||09:25 AM||||Me too. I finally got all the pieces to get my shifter stuff swapped. I got a 4 speed trans and had rigged the 5 speed shifter/cables. I swapped everything including the shift lever I had cut to rig an "extension". Both pivot pins were rusted solid in the brackets and the lever had to be cut off after breaking a 2 ton puller. I got my reverse lights wired to the shifter and after all that it drives like a new car. The 4 speed shifter came out of an 84 so its an inch or two shorter, nice positive feel now with correct cables and linkage! Next was a tune-up check - now I know why NOx emissions were so high and slightly rough idle. Some previous $%^#$ had stripped one of the dist cap screw holes and left the other screw loose so the whole cap would lift about an inch. On top of that they used the old style coil wire (internal terminal on the old oil filled coils) and it was just laying on the dist cap terminal. I got the snake oil Bosch +4 plugs outta there and put in some Rapidfire #1's and tapped a bigger size to tighten up the cap. A new coil wire and another wire that looked like it was seated last time with a chisel and WOW what a difference. It runs smooth and 3rd gear isn't grinding anymore WOOHOOO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
